.\" build time.
.TH HOURCALC 1 "2026-10-10" "HourCalc @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hourcalc \- convert hours between h:mm and decimal hours, and calculate with hours
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hourcalc
.RI [ option ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B HourCalc
converts hours between hours and minutes (08:30) and decimal hours (8.50), and calculates
with hours.
The converter tab has two fields side by side: type in either one and the other follows at
once.
The calculator tab adds and subtracts durations and multiplies and divides them by a
factor.
.PP
.B hourcalc
starts the front end that fits the desktop.
On KDE Plasma (\fBXDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP\fR contains KDE) it is the Qt 6 front end, on every
other desktop the GTK 4 and libadwaita one.
Both have the same tabs, keys and behaviour and use the widgets, fonts and colours of
their desktop.
Every argument is passed on to the front end unchanged.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage text and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the name and the version of the front end that was started
(for example "hourcalc-gtk 1.0.0") and exit.
.PP
The front ends also take the options of their toolkit (GTK and GLib:
.BR \-\-help\-all ;
Qt:
.BR \-style ", " \-platform ", ...)."
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOURCALC_UI
.B gtk
or
.B qt
(in any case) starts that front end whatever the desktop is.
If it is not installed the other one is started.
Any other value is ignored.
.TP
.B HOURCALC_RENDERER
GTK front end only.
Without a usable graphics device (no render node under
.IR /dev/dri ,
as in many virtual machines and remote sessions) the window is painted by the cairo
renderer, which is faster to start than GTK's GPU renderers running in software; with one,
GTK chooses.
.B gtk
leaves the choice to GTK in every case, any other value (for example
.BR cairo ", " ngl " or " vulkan )
is passed on to GTK as
.BR GSK_RENDERER ,
which wins over this variable when it is set.
.TP
.B XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP
Chooses the front end when
.B HOURCALC_UI
is not set.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the settings file lives, see
.BR FILES .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hourcalc/hourcalc.ini
The settings, usually
.IR ~/.config/hourcalc/hourcalc.ini .
It is made by the first change of a setting and holds one setting per line:
.B DecimalPlaces
(2 to 6, default 2) and
.B Theme
(\fBauto\fR, \fBlight\fR or \fBdark\fR, default \fBauto\fR, which follows the system).
Delete the file to go back to the defaults.
.TP
.I @LIBEXECDIR@/hourcalc-gtk
The GTK 4 and libadwaita front end.
.TP
.I @LIBEXECDIR@/hourcalc-qt
The Qt 6 front end.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B hourcalc
exits with the status of the front end it started, and with 127 when no front end is
installed.
